  <Groups>
    <Group elementId="CPLXQT-45" textLabel="D-lactate dehydrogenase" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLXQT-45" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>Biochemical characterization of the recombinant protein showed that At5g06580 encodes a D-lactate dehydrogenase (AtD-LDH). The recombinant protein is a homodimer with one FAD per monomer. Although AtD-LDH catalyzed the oxidation of D-lactate preferentially, it can also use L-lactate D-2-hydroxybutyrate, glycerate, and glycolate as substrates|CITS: [19586914]|.</Comment>
